  "id": "DrugBank_DB05271 - MONDO_10709",
  "verbalization": "Rotigotine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome through a series of pharmacological and pathophysiological links. The evidence suggests that Rotigotine is associated with X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome, a condition that in turn is linked to Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome. This implies a potential role of Rotigotine in the development or progression of this syndrome, possibly through mechanisms involving neurodegeneration or metabolic pathways. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Rotigotine to the syndrome highlights a potential overlap in pathophysiology, where Rotigotine may act as a mediator in the cascade of events leading to the manifestation of the syndrome. The consistent association across different indications underscores the importance of Rotigotine in this context, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
